      "subject": "CPU-to-Dcache/Mesh request routing",
      "explanation": "The CPU drive event is queued in cfifo0, then delayed (delaymux) before being presented to select1. select1 uses address decode signals (w_toCache_1, w_toMesh_1) to steer the event to either o_driveToDcache or o_driveToMesh. Free signals from the target (i_freeFromDcache, i_freeFromMesh) are routed back through select1 to cfifo0 and then to o_freeCPUFMux.",
